led during the mid-period of the Three Kingdoms era, defending Silla's borders against rivals like Baekje."}, {"sourceSlug": "samguk-sagi", "sourceName": "Samguk Sagi", "verb": "CANONIZES", "targetSlug": "michu-of-silla", "targetName": "Michu of Silla", "context": "The *Samguk Sagi*, a foundational Korean historical text compiled in the 12th century, details the reign and achievements of Michu of Silla."}], "places": [{"name": "Gyeongju, South Korea", "role": "Capital City"}, {"name": "Korean Peninsula, East Asia", "role": "Geographic Region"}, {"name": "Baekje, Korean Peninsula", "role": "Rival Kingdom"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Michu of Silla", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "michu-of-silla"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q488160", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michu_of_Silla"], "tags": ["Monarchs & Rulers", "political-systems", "empire-and-colonialism", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Michu's reign fundamentally altered Silla's political landscape by establishing the Kim clan as the dominant royal lineage, a dynasty that would rule for over 600 years and eventually unify the Korean peninsula. This dynastic shift provided essential stability for Silla's long-term development.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-10-26T07:05:03Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#40280582678", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Michu was the thirteenth ruler of the Korean state of Silla. He was the first king of the Kim clan to sit on the Silla throne; this clan would hold the throne for most of Silla's later history. He was the son of Gudo, a leading Silla general, and the sixth-generation descendant of the clan founder Kim Alji.", "newValue": "Michu of Silla (reigned 262–284 CE), the 13th monarch of the ancient Korean kingdom of Silla, ascended to the throne, marking a pivotal dynastic shift. His reign definitively established the Kim clan's supremacy, ending the previous Park and Seok lineage dominance and inaugurating a continuous Kim dynasty that would govern Silla for over 600 years. This foundational change profoundly shaped the kingdom's political structure and laid crucial groundwork for its eventual unification of the Korean peninsula.

Michu's ascension was not just a change of ruler but a critical consolidation of power for the Kim clan, traditionally associated with the Silla capital of Gyeongju. During his 22-year reign, he focused on internal stability and defense against external threats, particularly from the rival kingdom of Baekje. Historical records, such as the *Samguk Sagi*, recount his efforts to strengthen the agricultural base and improve the lives of common people, including policies to alleviate famine and reduce taxes. He also reportedly led successful military campaigns against invading forces, solidifying Silla's borders against its aggressive neighbors.

The most enduring legacy of Michu's reign is the entrenchment of the Kim clan on the Silla throne, providing the essential dynastic stability that underpinned Silla's later expansion and its eventual unification of the Three Kingdoms of Korea in the 7th century. His policies fostering internal cohesion and agricultural prosperity laid a vital groundwork for future Silla strength and sustained growth. The establishment of a more standardized patrilineal succession within the Kim clan after his death further minimized future succession disputes among competing aristocratic factions, contributing to long-term political continuity."}, {"timestamp": "2026-10-26T07:05:03Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#40280582678", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Classical era: flourishing of philosophical inquiry, imperial expansion, and codification of la", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "250 CE"}, {"title": "Dynastic succession and sovereign authority traditions", "type": "Idea", "year": "250 CE"}], "newValue": ["The growing power and influence of the Kim clan within Silla's aristocratic structure provided a strong base for Michu's ascension.", "The preceding instability and gradual weakening of the Park and Seok clans created an opportunity for a new dynastic power to emerge.", "Michu's lineage as a sixth-generation descendant of Kim Alji, the clan founder, lent significant traditional legitimacy to his claim to the throne."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-10-26T07:05:03Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#40280582678", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Established dynastic legacies and territorial boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "284 CE"}, {"title": "Contributed to enduring intellectual and institutional frameworks shaping subsequent civilizati", "type": "Movement", "year": "284 CE"}], "newValue": ["Michu's reign established the Kim clan as the dominant royal lineage in Silla, which endured for over six centuries.", "His polic